1. What are React Components?React components are independent, reusable building blocks used to construct user interfaces. Think of them like LEGO bricks — each component handles its own layout, styling, and logic, and they nest together to build complete applications.2. Components vs. Standard JavaScript FunctionsFeatureStandard JavaScript FunctionReact Function ComponentReturn ValuePrimitive values, objects, arrays, or functionsJSX (HTML-like syntax describing UI)NamingcamelCase (e.g., calculateScore())PascalCase (e.g., <CalculateScore/>)PurposePerforms general logic or calculationsGenerates and manages user interface elementsInvocationCalled directly: myFunction()Rendered in JSX: <MyComponent/>3. Types of ComponentsFunction Components: Plain JavaScript functions that take props and return JSX. Modern, lightweight, and the standard in React development.Class Components: ES6 classes extending React.Component that manage local state and lifecycle methods using a render() method.4. Class Component ExampleClass components require extending React.Component and using the mandatory render() method:JavaScriptimport React, { Component } from 'react';

class CalculateScoreClass extends Component {
  render() {
    const { Name, Total, goal } = this.props;
    const average = (Total / goal).toFixed(2);
    return (
      <div>
        <h2>{Name}'s Average Score: {average}</h2>
      </div>
    );
  }
}

export default CalculateScoreClass;
5. Function Component ExampleFunction components are cleaner and accept props directly as an argument:JavaScriptimport React from 'react';

function CalculateScore(props) {
  const average = (props.Total / props.goal).toFixed(2);
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>{props.Name}'s Average Score: {average}</h2>
    </div>
  );
}

export default CalculateScore;
6. What is a Component Constructor?In Class components, constructor(props) is a special method executed when the component is created. It serves two main purposes:Initializing local state: this.state = { score: 0 };Binding event handler methods to this.Note: Modern Function components do not use constructors; state is managed using the useState hook instead.7. What is the render() Function?The render() method is required in Class components. React calls render() to inspect what should be displayed on screen and return the corresponding JSX. It must be a pure function — meaning it should not modify component state or directly interact with the browser.